<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Function Notation — expanding f(a+h)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Let \(f(x) = {@fx@}\), where \(a\) and \(h\) are any two real numbers.</p>
<p>Find and fully expand \(f(a+h)\).</p>
<div>\(f(a+h) =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Function notation \(f(a+h)\) means the output of \(f\) when the input is the <strong>whole expression</strong> \(a+h\). Replace every \(x\) in \(f(x)\) by \((a+h)\), in brackets, then expand using \((a+h)^2 = a^2+2ah+h^2\) and collect like terms:</p>
\[ f(a+h) = {@p@}(a+h)^2+{@q@}(a+h)+{@r@} = {@p@}\left(a^2+2ah+h^2\right)+{@q@}a+{@q@}h+{@r@} = {@ta@}. \]
<p>Note that \(f(a+h) \neq f(a)+f(h)\) in general: a function does not "distribute" over addition unless it happens to be linear with no constant term. Note too that \((a+h)^2 \neq a^2+h^2\): the middle term \(2ah\) is easy to forget.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[p : rand_with_prohib(2,5,[]);          /* at least 2, so no "1(a+h)^2" in the displays */
q : rand_with_prohib(2,9,[]);
r : rand_with_prohib(1,9,[]);
fx : p*x^2+q*x+r;
ta : expand(subst(x=a+h,fx));
/* An equivalent but unexpanded form, for the form-check test. Simplification does not multiply out brackets. */
unexp : p*(a+h)^2+q*(a+h)+r;
/* Diagnostics: both differ from ta by a non-zero polynomial (2*p*a*h-r and 2*p*a*h), on every seed. */
wrong_linear : expand(subst(x=a,fx)) + expand(subst(x=h,fx));   /* f(a+h) = f(a)+f(h) misconception */
wrong_sq : expand(p*(a^2+h^2)+q*(a+h)+r);                       /* (a+h)^2 = a^2+h^2 */
/* Validator: the answer may only use the letters a and h. */
validate_ah(ex) := if every(lambda([v], member(v, [a, h])), listofvars(ex)) then "" else "Use only the letters a and h.";]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
